# Privacy Pack

Use this pack when the project handles personal data, user documents, private content, telemetry, logs, or analytics.

## Rules

- Do not print, commit, or persist sensitive user data.
- Keep logs allowlisted and generic.
- Do not send private content to external services unless explicitly approved.
- Redact paths, payloads, tokens, identifiers, and raw user content from reports.
- Add or update tests when privacy-sensitive logging or error handling changes.

## Verification

- Confirm logs and errors do not expose sensitive values.
- Record any telemetry or external-service impact.

